# Performance Rules

## Code splitting & loading
- Every page lazy-loaded: `React.lazy` + `<Suspense fallback={<PageSkeleton />}>`.
- Heavy libs (3D, video, PDF, charts) dynamic-imported at usage site.
- Preload next probable route on hover/focus.

## Renders
- No inline objects/arrays/functions as props to memoised children.
- Subscribe narrowly: `useAppSelector(s => s.game.phase)`, not whole slices.
- RTK Query: `selectFromResult` for narrow projections.
- Virtualise lists >100 items.
- Profile before adding `memo`/`useMemo` — measure.

## Real-time render budget
- Cap re-renders at ~30 fps for non-game UIs (60 fps for canvases).
- Batch WS-driven dispatches via `requestAnimationFrame` or a tick aggregator.
- Use `startTransition` for non-urgent updates.

## Bundle
- Critical path ≤180 KB gzipped; per-route chunk ≤80 KB.
- Tree-shake: named imports only (`import { x } from "lodash-es"`).
- Mark side-effect-free packages with `"sideEffects": false`.

## Web Vitals targets
- LCP ≤2.5 s, INP ≤200 ms, CLS ≤0.1, TTFB ≤800 ms.

## Defensive UI
- "Reconnecting…" banner when WS disconnects.
- Last-known-good values rendered with `aria-busy="true"` while stale.
- Queue or fail optimistic actions when socket is down.
